privacy policy

Warm Cottage respects your privacy. This policy explains what this app actually handles, where that information stays, and how you can delete it.

1. Scope
This policy applies to the Warm Cottage app for iOS. The app does not offer account registration, and it does not upload your chats, games, meals, notes, memories, or companion status to the developer’s servers.

2. Information stored on this device
To let the companion continue, the following is written only on the current device:
· Your name, the character’s name, first-launch record, and days together
· Mood, energy, fullness, tidiness, closeness, and other companion status
· Chats and saved messages
· Meal records, game records, and memories
· Notes, and the reminder time you set for a note
· Experience settings such as language, sound effects, and background music

This information is used on the device to show the room, continue conversations, remind you about notes, and keep companion status. The app does not use it for advertising or profiling.

3. Information the app does not collect
The app does not ask for location, contacts, camera, photos, or the microphone in order to collect personal information. It does not read your messages, call history, or content from other apps. Sound effects and videos play on the device only. The app does not record audio and does not upload sound.

4. Subscriptions and payment
Chat and mini games require an active membership. The plans are weekly and yearly. The price is the price shown on the membership page and on the App Store confirmation sheet when you purchase.
Apple processes the payment. The developer does not receive your name, card number, Apple ID password, or full payment account. The app uses only the purchase verified by Apple on this device to decide whether chat and mini games are available.
Restore Subscription asks Apple whether the current Apple Account still has an active subscription. It does not send your chats to Apple.

5. Local notifications
When you turn on a reminder for a note, the app asks for notification permission and delivers a local notification at the time you chose. The notification text stays on the device and is not sent to the developer. You can turn notifications off in the system settings.

6. Storage, deletion, and sharing
Companion content is kept in the app’s local storage. In Settings you can delete chats, games, meals, memories, and notes separately, or restore all data. Uninstalling the app deletes that local content.
Deleting local data does not cancel an Apple subscription. Charges, renewal, and cancellation follow the subscription record on the Apple Account.
The app has no ads and does not sell or share this information with third parties. Aside from what Apple requires to verify a subscription, the developer does not run a cloud service that stores this content.

7. Children
The app is intended for people who can read and agree to this policy themselves. If you are under the age of consent where you live, use the app only with a guardian’s permission.

8. Updates
If the product changes, this policy will be updated and shown on the in-app Privacy Policy page. Continuing to use the app means you have seen the updated policy.
